From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:27:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/37] LLHD Sig2Reg: memoize feeder narrowing, compose injects
 over muxes, split struct hulls

Three fixes that finish the whole-drive narrowing for real FSM-shaped
feeders, found on CVA6's load_unit (a 117-bit dcache request struct with 7
per-field continuous assigns plus one always_comb whole-struct drive):

1. Memoize tryNarrowFeeder per top-level call. Real mux trees share
   subtrees (an FSM's else-if chain reuses its default arm), and without a
   cache the recursion is exponential in sharing -- which is what forced the
   old depth cap of 8, too small for load_unit's ~12-deep chain. With the
   cache every node is visited once and the cap is a safety net at 64.

2. Compose injects over muxes. The chain helpers required an inject chain to
   bottom out DIRECTLY at a probe of the signal, but real RTL produces
   struct_inject(mux(inject-chain, inject-chain), field) -- per-state
   defaults muxed, with per-state overrides injected on top. A single inject
   is now handled generically: recurse on its BASE through the full
   narrowing and union in the injected range.

3. Split struct ranges at field boundaries. The mux union coalesces adjacent
   writes into hulls (load_unit writes kill_req and tag_valid, adjacent i1
   fields, arriving as one 2-bit range), and the struct reconstruction
   demanded exactly one field per range and abandoned the whole narrowing.
   Ranges are now split back along field boundaries and must tile exactly.

Fixing only one of the three changes nothing -- which is how the first two
landed unnoticed until the third was found; the intervals stayed full-width
through each intermediate state.

CVA6: load_unit, cva6_icache, decoder promote; combined with the
RemoveControlFlow and Deseq work the design reaches ZERO residual llhd
(0 of 142 modules, 301 registers). OpenC910 unchanged (4,787), ibex
byte-identical.
